  displayImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bfd9c01ea984f4d46aff53d020fbea13, type: 3}
  displayText: If you are in still water, your best swimming speed is 3 feet / second.
    <br> If the river Stynx flows against your swimming direction at 1 feet a second,
    <br> what is the equation (x=seconds swimming) that outputs feet swam up the
    moving stream?<br> The equation would have x be any # seconds you can swim at
    this best speed. <br> FeetSwam(for x seconds) =
  solutionImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bfd9c01ea984f4d46aff53d020fbea13, type: 3}
  solutionText: FeetSwam(for x seconds) = 2x
